on-arrival: electoral_reform_referendum_done = 1; electoral_reform_referendum_turnout = 56; electoral_reform_referendum_yes = 52; electoral_reform_stage = "referendum_won"; electoral_reform_result = "The Article 125 referendum passed with 52% Yes on 56% turnout"; public_trust += 4; kukiz_programme_credit += 12; news_headline = "A 52-percent Yes vote gives the JOW amendment a binding public mandate"

= April 2022 — 52 to 48

Turnout reaches **56%**, safely beyond the threshold for a binding Article 125
result. **52% vote Yes**. <span class="party party-pis"><b>PiS</b></span>
carries much of the countryside, <span class="party party-ko"><b>KO</b></span>
sells independent boundaries to its cities, and <span class="party
party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> spends the campaign repeating
that the parties have finally asked permission from the people they govern.

The referendum supplies a mandate, not a self-executing amendment. Article 96
still says Sejm elections are proportional. The same text must now pass both
chambers under Article 235.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the result to Parliament

